## Original Content
New Berkshire Hathaway CEO Greg Abel appears to be letting Warren Buffett and portfolio manager Ted Weschler make all the decisions on the company's equities.

## Summary
Despite Greg Abel taking over as CEO of Berkshire Hathaway, Warren Buffett and portfolio manager Ted Weschler appear to still be making the decisions on the company's stock investments. Abel seems to be delegating equity decision-making rather than controlling it himself.

## Key Points
- Greg Abel has assumed the role of Berkshire Hathaway CEO
- Warren Buffett continues to call the shots on stock investments despite stepping back from the CEO role
- Portfolio manager Ted Weschler is also actively involved in the company's equities decisions
- Abel appears to be letting others handle equity investment decisions rather than directing them himself


